---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaSection from '../../components/CtaSection.astro';
import { graph, breadcrumbs } from '../../lib/schema';
import { CALENDLY, EMAIL } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'AI Automation Services & Pricing | pocho.tech';
const description =
  'Automation audit ($500), custom builds from $1,500, and embedded retainers. One engineer, Erick Bonilla, on every project.';

const jsonLd = graph(breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Services', path: '/services' }]));
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/services" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Start with an audit or a build. Most clients stay.</h1>
      <p>
        Everything I sell is a version of the same thing: a working automation, built by me, running in your
        accounts. The difference is how much of the work you want me to do and how long you want me around.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three teams run twelve of my automations in production. Every one of those engagements started on one of
        the rungs below.
      </p>
      <a href={CALENDLY} class="btn btn-primary" rel="noopener">Book a discovery call</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="ladder-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="ladder-h">The engagement ladder</h2>
      <div class="ladder">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>1. Automation Audit: $500, credited toward a build</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Who it's for:</strong> You know the hours are going somewhere, but you want a plan in writing
            before spending $1,500 or more.
          </p>
          <p>
            A 60-minute review of how your team actually works, then a written report within five business days:
            what to automate first, which tools, estimated time savings, and a build scope for each recommendation.
            Commission a build afterward and the full $500 comes off the price.
          </p>
          <p class="card-links">
            <a href="/services/automation-audit">About the audit</a> ·
            <a href={CALENDLY} rel="noopener">Book an audit</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>2. Custom Automation Build: from $1,500</h3>
          <p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> You can already name the process that's eating the hours.</p>
          <p>
            I design the solution, build and test it on your systems, and hand it off with documentation and a
            recorded walkthrough. Fixed price set in writing after a discovery call; typical timeline is one to
            four weeks.
          </p>
          <p>
            The proposal-to-invoice pipeline at an event production agency is one of these: processing went from
            1.5–2 hours per proposal to 15 minutes.
          </p>
          <p class="card-links">
            <a href="/services/custom-automation">About custom builds</a> ·
            <a href={CALENDLY} rel="noopener">Book a discovery call</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>3. Ongoing embedded work: scoped per engagement</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Who it's for:</strong> Teams that want an automation engineer on the roster without making a
            hire.
          </p>
          <p>
            I stay on after handoff, inside your Slack, your CRM, your boards, maintaining what's live and
            building what's next. This is how most of my work runs: all three client teams on this site continue
            on retainers.
          </p>
          <p>
            That's how one automation at the events agency became four, and one system at an EdTech
            workforce-training company became six.
          </p>
          <blockquote>
            <p>"You have done such a great job that I can't remember how we were working before you."</p>
            <cite>CEO, EdTech workforce-training company</cite>
          </blockquote>
          <p class="card-links">
            <a href={CALENDLY} rel="noopener">Book a discovery call</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="consulting-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="consulting-h">Prefer to build in-house?</h2>
      <p>
        For teams that want to build in-house: architecture review, workflow builds, self-hosting guidance,
        and training. A travel media company hired me to build after I taught n8n to their AI Advocacy
        Director.
      </p>
      <p class="card-links"><a href="/services/n8n-consulting">About n8n &amp; Make.com consulting</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="compare-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="compare-h">How the options compare</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="compare-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <td></td>
              <th scope="col">Working with pocho.tech</th>
              <th scope="col">Hiring an ops person</th>
              <th scope="col">Doing it yourself on Zapier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Cost</th>
              <td>From $1,500 per build, fixed in writing; retainers scoped per engagement</td>
              <td>A full-time salary, plus recruiting and ramp-up</td>
              <td>The subscription, plus your own hours</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Time to a working system</th>
              <td>One to four weeks from approved scope</td>
              <td>Months before the first build ships</td>
              <td>Fast for a two-step trigger; slow for multi-system pipelines with AI steps</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Who does the work</th>
              <td>One engineer with twelve automations in production</td>
              <td>A generalist whose week includes much more than automation</td>
              <td>You, between everything else on your plate</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">What you keep</th>
              <td>Workflows in your accounts, documented, with a recorded walkthrough</td>
              <td>Institutional knowledge that leaves with the employee</td>
              <td>Workflows only you understand</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="compare-note">
        If a simple Zapier trigger genuinely covers your case, you'll hear that on the discovery call.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSection
    heading="Where to start"
    body="If you can name the broken process, book the discovery call. It's the first step of every build. If you can't, the audit turns sixty minutes into a written plan, credited in full if you go ahead. If you'd rather see the work before talking to me, the case studies show it running."
  />
  <div class="cta-postscript">
    <p>Or write to me directly: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero h1 { max-width: 22ch; }
  .hero p { max-width: 62ch; }
  .hero .btn { margin-top: 18px; }

  .ladder {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .ladder .card h3 { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .card-links {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .card-links a { color: var(--c-text-mute); }
  .card-links a:hover { color: var(--c-text); }

  blockquote {
    margin: 20px 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--c-border);
  }
  blockquote p {
    color: var(--c-text);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  cite {
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--c-text-dim);
  }

  .table-scroll {
    margin-top: 32px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .compare-table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 760px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    background: var(--c-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }
  .compare-table th,
  .compare-table td {
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    color: var(--c-text-body);
  }
  .compare-table thead th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--c-text);
    background: var(--c-bg-deep);
  }
  .compare-table thead td { background: var(--c-bg-deep); }
  .compare-table tbody th[scope='row'] {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--c-text);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .compare-note {
    margin-top: 24px;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
  }

  .cta-postscript {
    background: var(--c-surface-alt);
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: calc(-1 * var(--space-section) + 32px);
    padding-bottom: calc(var(--space-section) - 32px);
  }
  .cta-postscript p {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: none;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }
</style>
